[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mReturn it, don't pass it (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mNo signature change. login() returns { success, user, userId } and the submit handler logs it. Matches how a real [39m
     [38;5;246mauth API works: identity is the output of login, not an input.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Caller-supplied tracking ID
     [38;5;246mlogin(username, password, userId) where userId is a correlation/trace ID generated per attempt, so failed logins [39m
     [38;5;246mare traceable too. Not the account identity.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Third param from the form
     [38;5;246mlogin(username, password, userId) with a new userId field added to index.html for the user to supply. Literally [39m
     [38;5;246mwhat was asked, but touches the form and asks the user for an ID pre-auth.[39m
